 "steps": [
  {
   "id": "s0",
   "title": "Read the question",
   "text": "Define the cross (vector) product and list its properties.",
   "actions": []
  },
  {
   "id": "s1",
   "title": "Definition",
   "text": "\\( \\vec A\\times\\vec B = AB\\sin\\theta\\,\\hat n \\) (Eq 2.15). \\( \\hat n \\) is perpendicular to the plane of A and B: curl the right-hand fingers from the first vector to the second through the smaller angle, the thumb gives \\( \\hat n \\). The result is a **vector**.",
   "actions": []
  },
  {
   "id": "s2",
   "title": "Properties 1–2",
   "text": "(1) **Not commutative**: \\( \\vec A\\times\\vec B = -\\vec B\\times\\vec A \\). (2) **Parallel or anti-parallel** vectors (and a vector with itself) give the null vector: \\( \\hat i\\times\\hat i = \\hat j\\times\\hat j = \\hat k\\times\\hat k = 0 \\).",
   "actions": []
  },
  {
   "id": "s3",
   "title": "Properties 3",
   "text": "(3) **Perpendicular** vectors give the maximum \\( |\\vec A\\times\\vec B| = AB \\). Cyclic order: \\( \\hat i\\times\\hat j = \\hat k,\\; \\hat j\\times\\hat k = \\hat i,\\; \\hat k\\times\\hat i = \\hat j \\); reversing the order gives a minus sign.",
   "actions": []
  },
  {
   "id": "s4",
   "title": "Property 4: determinant",
   "text": "\\( \\vec A\\times\\vec B = (A_yB_z - A_zB_y)\\hat i + (A_zB_x - A_xB_z)\\hat j + (A_xB_y - A_yB_x)\\hat k \\). Examples: torque \\( \\vec r\\times\\vec F \\), angular momentum \\( \\vec r\\times\\vec p \\).",
   "actions": []
  }
 ],
 "formulas": [
  {
   "title": "Cross product",
   "tex": "\\vec A\\times\\vec B = AB\\sin\\theta\\,\\hat n",
   "text": "Eq 2.15; magnitude AB sin θ, direction by the right-hand rule."
  }
 ],
